# AYRA — example settings file
# ===================================================================
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. AYRA runs with no settings file at all: the
# brain uses your Claude login, and voice falls back to the browser's speech.
#
# To change something: copy this file to .env.local (same folder), then
# uncomment and edit only the lines you need. .env.local is gitignored —
# never commit a real key.
#
# Two programs read .env.local:
#   - the BRIDGE (the brain, bridge/server.mjs) reads AYRA_* and ELEVENLABS_API_KEY
#   - the FACE (the Vite web app) reads VITE_* — and only VITE_* values ever
#     reach the browser, so never put a secret in a VITE_ variable.
#
# Who AYRA is (name, wake words, honorific, language, voice gender) is NOT set
# here — that lives in config/identity.json.


# ===================================================================
# BRIDGE (the brain)
# ===================================================================

# Model for the brain. Default claude-opus-5-5 (smartest).
# claude-sonnet-5-5 answers faster and uses less of your Claude plan.
# AYRA_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# Reasoning effort: low | medium | high | xhigh | max. Default medium.
# AYRA_EFFORT=medium

# Port the brain listens on (WebSocket + HTTP). Default 8787.
# If you change it, change VITE_BRIDGE_URL below to match.
# AYRA_BRIDGE_PORT=8787

# Reloading the page continues the last conversation if it was used within
# this many hours; older ones start fresh. Default 6.
# AYRA_RESUME_HOURS=6

# claude.ai connectors (from your Claude account) AYRA may READ, comma
# separated, or "none". They can never send, reply, trash or share until
# Approve/Deny confirmations exist. Connectors not listed are removed from
# AYRA's sessions entirely. Default: none — today AYRA searches the web only,
# and each connector comes back as its own step (PLAN.md).
# AYRA_CONNECTORS=none

# Extra web-page origins allowed to talk to the brain, comma separated.
# Local dev addresses (localhost:5173-5199, 4173-4199) are already allowed.
# AYRA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Allow clients that send no Origin header at all (scripts, native apps).
# Off by default, because that is also what local malware looks like.
# AYRA_ALLOW_NO_ORIGIN=0

# Laptop control (the owner's choice): AYRA runs PowerShell, edits files and
# drives her Chrome; spending money, sending as you, deleting for good and
# passwords/security wait for your Approve. 0 = reading only.
# AYRA_ALLOW_WRITES=1

# Her Chrome ("Chrome (AYRA)", made by `npm run shortcuts`): the remote-control
# port, and where chrome.exe is if it isn't in the usual place.
# AYRA_CHROME_PORT=9222
# AYRA_CHROME_PATH=

# Sites where AYRA may allow the microphone, camera, notifications or location
# by herself, comma separated (localhost is always trusted). Others ask you.
# AYRA_TRUSTED_SITES=meet.google.com,web.whatsapp.com

# The brain's Claude process sleeps after this many idle minutes (0 = never).
# AYRA_SLEEP_MINUTES=10

# ElevenLabs voice id. Default: the voice in config/identity.json (Lily).
# AYRA_VOICE_ID=

# 1 = print every message from the Claude Agent SDK (troubleshooting).
# AYRA_DEBUG=0

# ElevenLabs API key (optional): premium voice + speech-to-text.
# Free tier is enough to try it. If your elevenlabs MCP server in
# ~/.claude.json already has a key, the bridge finds it there too.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=


# ===================================================================
# TELEGRAM (reach AYRA from your phone — PLAN.md Phase 3)
# ===================================================================

# Your bot's token from @BotFather (looks like 123456789:AA...). Secret.
# AYRA_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=

# Your own Telegram user ID — AYRA answers this account and nobody else.
# Filled in during setup, after you send /start to your bot.
# AYRA_TELEGRAM_OWNER_ID=

# off = this process doesn't answer Telegram (for a second, test-only bridge).
# AYRA_TELEGRAM=on


# ===================================================================
# FACE (the web app)
# ===================================================================

# Where the brain listens. Keep the port in step with AYRA_BRIDGE_PORT.
# VITE_BRIDGE_URL=ws://localhost:8787
